Z||000000||jch82||09-20-2001||01:48 AM||||My zr-1 hood scoop should be here in the next couple days. I am planning on picking up another hood from the junkyard and put it on that one so I can still drive my fiero around.<P>What I'm wondering is what I should use to cut out the hole in the hood to make it functional??? I know it has to be just behind the radiator, but what type of saw do I use??<P>Has anyone tried SEM Fast Set Adhesive?? It is made specifically for hood scoops, etc.... This is what the lady at the paint store recommended. Also, should I use the flexible or rigid parts repair (also made by SEM) to glass the scoop in after I adhere it with the adhesive?? Thanks!!<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jch82(sig).jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fiero_Freak||09-20-2001||04:48 AM||||   I hope you didn't buy that from Fieromen or Outlaw Performance?  Otherwise you may want to wait and see if you get the part befor you guy the adhesive.  As far as the glassing I would use the flexible, I've heard the rigid will pop out.||||reg||1
